  "TEST_used": false,
  "scope": "Previous completed shared-diffusion 1000-update adaptation: three fixed EXO development VAL windows, clean/noisy before/after. Not a representative validation or TEST benchmark. Predictions unchanged.",
  "units": "All joint positions/rest in metres. Native trajectory/translation/direct-joint feature channels are /2; FK multiplies translation by2 and rest already contains calibrated native body scale. Never multiply rest by body_scale again.",
  "interpretation": [
    "Visible similarity fits do not use GT; a single robust transform pools the complete window. Fitted scale is a diagnostic and can include trajectory/articulation error, not necessarily body-size error.",
    "Observable parent-child bone/rest length ratios isolate metrical body-size consistency from translation and rigid orientation. Ratios near1 indicate no unit/body-size mismatch for those measured bones.",
    "All GT-fitted metrics are labelled diagnostic_gt_*. There are no per-frame rigid/similarity GT fits; root-relative error is explicitly a translation-removed articulation diagnostic.",
    "The first new residual-adapter trial keeps body/rest fixed. Using GT-similarity scores as corrected predictions would hide global metric/root errors and violate the intended calibrated-scene protocol.",
    "GT Kabsch/Umeyama minimizes squared distance/RMS, not mean Euclidean MPJPE. Thus the aligned mean distance can increase although the window RMS decreases. Both metrics are reported; neither replaces the official unaligned metric."
  ],
